# Project Structure

The project follows a feature-based organization with clear separation of concerns:

Core Structure:
- src/
  - ui/
    - components/ (Reusable UI components)
    - hooks/ (Custom React hooks)
  - types/ (TypeScript type definitions)
  - data/ (Static data and mock files)

Component Organization:
- Each component should have its own directory
- Use index.ts for clean exports
- Tests go in __tests__ directory
- One component per file

Example Files:
- [src/App.tsx](mdc:src/App.tsx) - Main application component
- [src/ui/components/Movies/Movies.tsx](mdc:src/ui/components/Movies/Movies.tsx) - Movie component
- [src/ui/hooks/useMovies.ts/useMovies.ts](mdc:src/ui/hooks/useMovies.ts/useMovies.ts) - Movies hook
- [src/types/movie.ts](mdc:src/types/movie.ts) - Movie type definitions

Imports:
- Use @ alias for src directory
- Group imports by: React, external libraries, internal modules
- Use named exports over default exports
